-   entry #Input   `<input>`: a form control; a void tag with a preset for every `type`
+   entry #Input
+     info
+         `<input>` : un contrôle de formulaire ; une balise vide avec un préréglage pour chaque
+         `type`

-     detail
-         A `Tag.Void` whose `Topic` is `"input"`. `Input` alone is an input with no `type`
-         (a text field); each member presets `type`, so `Input.Email(name = t"email")` is
-         `<input type="email" name="email">`, and the parser reads `<input type="button">`
-         back as `Input.Button`. An input takes `name`, `value`, `disabled`, `readonly`,
-         `required`, `checked`, `placeholder`, `autocomplete`, `list`, `min`, `max`, `step`,
-         `pattern`, `size`, `maxlength`, `minlength`, `multiple`, `accept`, `alt`, `src`,
-         `width`, `height`, `form`, `formaction` and its siblings, `dirname`, `popovertarget`
-         and `popovertargetaction`.
+     detail
+         Un `Tag.Void` dont le `Topic` est `"input"`. `Input` seul est une entrée sans `type` (un
+         champ de texte) ; chaque membre prérègle `type`, de sorte que
+         `Input.Email(name = t"email")` vaut `<input type="email" name="email">`, et l'analyseur
+         relit `<input type="button">` en `Input.Button`. Une entrée prend `name`, `value`,
+         `disabled`, `readonly`, `required`, `checked`, `placeholder`, `autocomplete`, `list`,
+         `min`, `max`, `step`, `pattern`, `size`, `maxlength`, `minlength`, `multiple`, `accept`,
+         `alt`, `src`, `width`, `height`, `form`, `formaction` et ses semblables, `dirname`,
+         `popovertarget` et `popovertargetaction`.

=         and `popovertargetaction`.
